      "analysis_required": "Complete ten-piece later root saved before promotion. f8=B/Be6 is actual ten-piece stalemate: the promoted bishop is pinned to Kh8 by Rc8, and all white pawns/king are blocked. f8=Q/Be6/Qxc8/Bxc8 is legal and not stalemate; fxg8=N+/Rxg8+/Kxg8/a2 is legal but its outcome is not certified. The knight promotion captures on g8, whereas bishop and queen promotions are on f8. Prove the draw objective against every Black defense to f8=B, with a3/g5/g7 and White g4/h5 retained. One actual stalemate does not prove the full root is drawn."
